WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.360
Deep in tropical jungles 
lie floating kingdoms,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.340
ruled by beautiful and deadly masters.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.720
They're sort of the high elves
of the ant kingdoms;

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.100
talented architects that
create castles and city-states.

00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:18.920
But they are also fierce
and expansionist warriors,

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.260
and their kingdoms are ensnared
in a never-ending war for survival.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.900
'Oecophylla Weaver Ants'

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.760
[Intro music]

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.720
Oecophylla weavers walk on long legs,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.780
have slender bodies, and large eyes,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.600
which make them look pretty cute.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.620
Although, their strong mandibles
and the ability to shoot acid

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.040
also make them pretty good at killing.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.840
But more on that later.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.200
Their colonies usually have
two to three worker classes

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.120
that vary dramatically in size:

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.300
majors, minors, and sometimes
even tiny minim workers.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.140
Depending on location and species,

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.380
they vary in color from dark
brown to emerald green.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.400
Other than their fancy looks,
what makes weavers special

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.260
is that they're in the
kingdom-building business.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.160
They like to build at
pretty much all heights,

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.940
starting in shrubs a few
centimeters above the ground,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.400
and up to 10 meters in the tree canopy.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.620
But, they're not satisfied
with ruling just one plant.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.100
Weavers will look for twigs or lianas
that bridge the gap to other trees,

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.820
and expand to every plant they can reach.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.320
This way, colonies spread upwards
and sideways through the treetops.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.200
The largest weaver ant
kingdoms we know of

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.000
occupy up to 1,600 square meters,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.280
around four basketball courts,

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.260
a lot of ground to cover for tiny ants,

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.480
and impossibly hard to control.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:57.160
So, weaver ants construct dozens of
nests scattered all over their territory:

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.280
outposts to defend the kingdom,

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.640
tubes or balls made from leaves,
and ghostly silk sheets.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.340
These masterpieces
of high-ant architecture

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.440
are created by the weaver majors,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.200
the larger worker ants, which are
responsible for the more dangerous jobs

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.680
like fighting, foraging,
and nest construction.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.580
To start a new nest,

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.440
a major tries to bend different leaves
in her surroundings into a tube.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.480
If one of the leaves is flexible enough,
more workers will arrive to help.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:30.000
Chains of workers pull
the leaf's edges together

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.660
or reach across gaps and grab distant
leaves to add them to the construction.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.600
While the bending and pulling is going on,

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:41.680
other workers carry larvae from the
closest nest to the construction site.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.380
Usually, ant larvae spin themselves
a cocoon to protect themselves.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.580
But the weaver ant larvae give all of their
silk to the colony as building material.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.020
So, when the workers tap the
larvae's heads on the leaf,

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.640
they release their sticky thread
like tiny, cute glue guns.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.280
This way, the workers sew the bent leaf
onto itself so it won't unfold anymore.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.980
This creates a central chamber,

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.560
that's used as the basis for up to 300
more leaves that are wound around it.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.100
Together, they form little pockets and act
as additional rooms for the new outpost.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:19.260
To make it even more cozy,

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:23.280
minor workers use the larvae to weave
additional floors and chambers.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:27.560
Nests are usually constructed as
barracks on the territory's borders,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.340
or as storage for brood and food supplies.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.600
This way, the ants don't need to cross
vast distances to the headquarters,

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.820
but have soldiers close to
any potential point of conflict.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.280
Apart from one special nest
in the middle of the network,

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.660
which is reserved for the
queen and her guards.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.520
Here, she produces
hundreds of eggs a day,

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.840
which get transferred to suitable
nests with brood chambers.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.960
So, a colony is a network
of little castles and moats,

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:58.360
connected by suspension bridges
made from leaves, lianas, and twigs.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.080
An established colony easily has half a
million individuals that need to be fed.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.800
Fortunately, weaver ants
evolve to have very close

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.280
and beneficial relationships
with their hosts:

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.800
shrubs and trees.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.740
The tree gives the ants a home
and access to sweet sap to drink.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.640
But maybe even more importantly,
it allows them to cultivate cattle,

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.860
like aphids or caterpillars, that
produce honeydew for them.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.100
This would usually hurt a tree,

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.480
but these insects belong
to a small group of VIPs.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.500
Only a few selected neighbours and the
ants' cattle are allowed on the fruit tree.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.660
Many other insects, and even
larger herbivores are scared off,

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.980
or even killed and eaten.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:46.340
So in most cases, the tree only has to
tolerate acceptable levels of damage

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:49.020
while being protected from
more dangerous pests.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:54.740
The weaver ant kingdom could be an
ant paradise if there wasn't competition,

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.180
mostly from other kingdoms.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.960
Just like medieval humans,

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.640
every queen seeks to conquer others
and make their land their own.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.760
Controlling fertile land is the
key to survive in the jungle.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.480
And if a kingdom loses too much of it, it
shrinks and is overrun or starves to death.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.140
So expanding and defending their borders
is critical to keep the colony alive.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.740
When a kingdom invades another,

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.700
it first gathers an army of
a few thousand majors

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.400
who make their way towards
the opposing colony.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.920
The goal is to steal a bit of
territory and take it over.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:33.300
Defending weaver patrols
quickly spot the invaders

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.020
and immediately release
an alarm pheromone.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.480
Some rush to the front to defend,

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:41.300
while others rush to the
closest outposts for help,

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.300
marking their route with pheromones.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.520
Whenever they meet other sisters,

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.620
they jerk their bodies as if in a fight,

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.680
to signal them to follow the
pheromone trail to the front line.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.380
At the site of battle, majors from
both parties raise their bodies,

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.720
circle each other with
mandibles wide open,

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.020
and try to seize their opponents.

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.200
If an ant gets a hold of her opponent,

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:06.220
the victim is pulled into a group of
allied majors and pinned down.

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.160
The ants then rip the victim apart,

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.260
clipping off antennae and legs,

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.440
and slicing open their abdomens.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.220
To slow down the advance of the attackers,

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:19.640
the defending majors squirt
formic acid over the battlefield,

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.960
to chemically burn their targets.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:25.320
This is soon answered in the
same way by the attackers.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.400
In the chaotic battle,

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.740
both parties lose countless fighters
on the increasingly acidic battlefield.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.800
After a few minutes, the backup
from the outposts arrive,

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:39.240
and the time window for a
successful attack slowly closes.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.720
This is when the battle turns.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.000
The defenders slowly push
back the attack party.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.080
In the end, the attackers can't
keep up and have to retreat.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:52.660
For both parties, it was a costly battle.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.840
Thousands of corpses lie piled up
on the ground under the battlefield,

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.360
and many ants are severely injured.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.540
The defending colony's nests
and brood are safe though.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:08.100
The attackers' attempt to steal
new valuable territory has failed...

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.120
...for today.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.260
They'll try again soon.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.820
But the kingdom will be ready.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.820
For the high ants of
the floating kingdoms,

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.320
war is nothing special.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.080
It's just a fact of life.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:24.340
Because as we know, empires
never, ever have enough.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.280
And the weaver ants are ready to fight.

